&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-unfolded-link&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;collapsible-block-link&quot; href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;-&amp;nbsp;This&amp;nbsp;Is&amp;nbsp;Not&amp;nbsp;A&amp;nbsp;Place&amp;nbsp;of&amp;nbsp;Honor&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-content&quot;&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The Hector Rosales that appears in this is the father of Achilles Rosales, who appears in 3477 as the commander of the MTF that&#039;s hunting down the Harold Holts. The family has a thing for Homeric names.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Caceres might be the serpent from the Garden of Eden, or some variation of a Prometheus figure. It&#039;s extradimensional, so it&#039;s very likely and possible that it served that role on another plane of existence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This went through a HEAVY set of revisions
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;was more complex, tons of subdesignations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;eigenweapon was a reveal, rather than a lead&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;actual weapon was WAY DIF&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;upside down thing still canon &amp;#8212; just didnt have room to fit it in&lt;/li&gt;
